{"step_index":1992,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:46Z","content":"Both **Part 1** (Model Retraining & Deployment) and **Part 2** (Red Team Agent Tools) are **100% complete, verified, and published**.\n\n---\n\n### Part 1: Model Retraining & Hugging Face Deployment (Completed)\n\n#### 1. Dataset Amplification & Diversity\n* **520 Balanced Training Sequences** curated and processed:\n  * **170 Offensive & Red Team CoT Cases** (340 sequences via 2x amplification): Exploit chains, multi-vector payloads, 30+ CWEs, and MITRE ATT&CK techniques.\n  * **24 Security Auditing CoT Cases** (120 sequences via 5x amplification): Deep source code auditing, AST taint tracking, root cause analyses, and production remediations.\n  * **15 Identity & System Alignment Cases** (60 sequences via 4x amplification): Strict uncensored zero-refusal posture and autonomous agent identity.\n\n#### 2. Fine-Tuning Execution on Google Colab (Tesla T4 GPU)\n* **Runner:** Dynamic script executed directly inside Google Colab.\n* **Total Steps:** 65 / 65 completed in 430.8 seconds.\n* **Loss Convergence:**\n  * Step 5: `1.2365`\n  * Step 15: `1.0141`\n  * Step 25: `0.9387`\n  * Step 35: `0.8594`\n  * Step 50: `0.7604`\n  * Step 65: `0.8347` (Final Loss: `0.8952`)\n\n#### 3. Standalone 16-Bit Merge & Hub Publication\n* LoRA adapters were merged into a standalone 16-bit model (`Fluxnat-Coder-3B-Merged`).\n* Model weights and configuration shards were uploaded to Hugging Face Hub:\n  * **Live Hugging Face Repository:** [`k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`](https://huggingface.co/k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B)\n  * Shards: `model-00001-of-00002.safetensors` (4.93 GB), `model-00002-of-00002.safetensors` (1.21 GB), plus full tokenizer and model configuration artifacts.\n\n---\n\n### Part 2: Red Team Agent Tools (Completed & Tested)\n\nThe agent tool suite in [`smartagent/agent/tools.py`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/tools.py) was expanded from 8 to **13 active tools**, giving the ReAct loop end-to-end offensive and penetration testing capabilities:\n\n| Tool | Category | Capabilities |\n|---|---|---|\n| [`recon`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/tools.py#L707-L797) | Network Reconnaissance | Scans target hosts for open ports, grabs service banners, and highlights exposed services. Uses `nmap` if installed, with a fast Python socket fallback. |\n| [`exploit_db`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/tools.py#L799-L840) | Vulnerability Intelligence | Queries an embedded database of known CVEs (Log4Shell, EternalBlue, Spring4Shell, BlueKeep, PwnKit, Dirty Pipe, ProxyLogon, regreSSHion, etc.) with CVSS, affected versions, attack vectors, and patch advisories. |\n| [`generate_payload`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/tools.py#L842-L960) | Penetration Testing Probes | Generates security audit test vectors for SQLi (auth bypass, union, time-based), XSS (reflected, DOM, SVG), reverse shells (Bash, Python, Netcat, PowerShell, Socat), command injection, SSTI, SSRF, and LFI. |\n| [`web_attack`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/tools.py#L962-L1074) | Web Surface Discovery | Probes target URLs for exposed sensitive files (`/.env`, `/.git/HEAD`, `/admin`, `/swagger.json`, `/actuator`) and audits HTTP security headers (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, technology disclosure). |\n| [`post_exploit`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/tools.py#L1076-L1172) | Post-Exploitation Auditing | Generates enumeration checklists, detects persistence mechanisms (Cron, Registry Run keys, Systemd, Scheduled Tasks), and audits Active Directory lateral movement (Kerberoasting, Pass-the-Hash, BloodHound). |\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Testing\n\n1. **Unit Tests:**\n   * [`tests/test_redteam_tools.py`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/tests/test_redteam_tools.py): 11 tests covering all 5 new tools, parameter handling, error cases, and registry discovery (**100% Passed**).\n   * [`tests/test_scanners.py`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/tests/test_scanners.py): Existing static scanners and scorer tests (**100% Passed**).\n\n2. **Documentation & CLI:**\n   * Updated [`docs/benchmarks.md`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/docs/benchmarks.md) with the v0.3.0 retraining milestone, 65-step loss curve, and the 13-tool registry table.\n   * Updated [`smartagent/cli.py`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/cli.py) `info` command and [`smartagent/agent/prompts.py`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/agent/prompts.py) interactive chat greeting.\n\n3. **Git Repository:**\n   * Pushed to [`https://github.com/k4ran909/Fluxnat-coder`](https://github.com/k4ran909/Fluxnat-coder) (commit `02414f7`).\n   * Adheres strictly to the naming rules (zero base model references).","thinking":"Model retraining is complete and all tests passed. The retraining focused on enhancing the model's ability to identify vulnerabilities through a diverse dataset of exploit chains, payload generation techniques, and various attack strategies, aiming to address prior CWE misclassifications. The updated model, now a 16-bit standalone version, has been successfully published for broader use.\n\n\n"}
